{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30035 - PROTEIN:5814",
  "verbalization": "Erysimoside is implicated in a mechanistic pathway that leads to the activation of VMRC-MELG, a target of multiple metabolic intermediates. The evidence suggests that Erysimoside acts as a modulator of the SDR family member 9, which is a dehydrogenase/reductase enzyme involved in the metabolism of various compounds. This enzyme is targeted by two distinct metabolites, 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and 6-Hydroxy-2-[2-(2-hydroxyphenyl) ethyl]chromone, both of which are themselves targets of Erysimoside. These intermediates ultimately converge on VMRC-MELG, indicating a potential regulatory role for Erysimoside in the metabolic pathways leading to VMRC-MELG activation. The consistent presence of Erysimoside as a target of multiple metabolic intermediates, coupled with the shared target VMRC-MELG, suggests a possible role in modulating the activity of the SDR family member 9, which could have implications for downstream biological processes. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Erysimoside to influence VMRC-MELG through a complex network of metabolic interactions.",
